roof file tests/test_spec_obligation_gate.py plus the fixture PAIR (type-only / method-only / neither) are named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm. Gate: worktree PASS 625 passed / 2 skipped 901.55s; merged main PASS 625 passed / 2 skipped 917.00s rc 0 (transcripts ~/.hermes/goals/sg9-wt-gate-r2.log, ~/.hermes/goals/sg9-main-gate.log).\n\nCLOSED on a commit-bound GitReins PASS. Task AUG-150 created with the row's four acceptance criteria as separate criteria (PROOF/FAILIF each); 'gitreins judge AUG-150' at HEAD 6009e742839e172daa465e9af09b30d77c6a220d (contains fix 7463dec, ancestor proven) -> pass_class=judged, tier1 PASS (secrets+lint+tests: full gate 722 passed / 2 skipped in 871.92s, GATE PASS, LIVE ARMS ran 2 skipped 0), tier2 COMPLETE 7/7 items PASS (4 authored + 3 derived), zero ungraded. Artifact .gitreins/history/2026-11-11/a9b1feeb/verdict.json (task_id=AUG-150, commit=6009e74); CLI printed 'Verdict saved: e2e3196b' but the directory is a9b1feeb, resolved by matching task_id AND commit. Driver re-measured the premise before dispatch: type-stripped specs/ copy with spec-verbs.xml path mutated to tests/does-not-exist.py refused rc 2 stale-test-ref by BOTH spec validate and spec check naming document+block+resolved path; shipped corpus validates ok; tests/test_spec_obligation_gate.py 12 passed in 1.82s, named in tests/gate.sh arm line 206.", "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": [], "worktree": "/home/kara/proj-wt-auger-xml-hardening", "branch": "wt/auger-xml-hardening", "commit_hash": "7463dec9f9009c6fe63bd8df413165ca1dc7ac57", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP"}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-151", "title": "docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md's worked example is invalid: it declares verifies on both sides, which the loader refuses as a reference cycle", "detail": {"fingerprint": "6a8249915983211a6a1d2066c34ca9d11d856b6227eca38b1c87b991809ed858"}, "priority": "P3", "source": null, "reasoning": "Found while authoring the corpus (AUG-136). The example shows a requirement with verifies=\"TEST\" AND the verification block with verifies=\"REQ\". The loader treats that mutual edge as `reference-cycle` (rc 2, reproduced on a scratch document) because the closure walk follows verifies in both directions. An author who copies the documented example gets a refusal with no hint that the documentation is the cause. Measured: one-directional edges (requirement owns verifies=verification) validate; the mutual shape is refused.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: docs/XML-SPEC-SCHEMA.md's example is a document that `auger spec validate` accepts, proven by a test that extracts the fenced example (or a copy of it) and validates it.\nPASS: the document states the edge rule in one sentence: verifies is declared on one side only (which side), and a mutual declaration is a cycle — with the refusal text quoted.\nPASS: if the loader is instead changed to accept the mutual shape (a defensible choice), the cycle detector's rule is updated and a test pins the new behaviour — but the doc and the code must agree either way.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.534751+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.534751+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": []}
 {"status": "pending", "id": "AUG-152", "title": "`spec check` omits acceptance blocks from its node list, so a verified acceptance is invisible to the verb that reports the graph", "detail": {"fingerprint": "16f21a6f000adfa26db15b616fbf47845ca12af7492fc3df39cce5d09b5b4b2b"}, "priority": "P4", "source": null, "reasoning": "Found while authoring the corpus (AUG-136). SPEC_BLOCK_TAGS covers requirement/verification/test but not acceptance, so a corpus whose requirement has an acceptance block reports only the requirement and verification ids: the authored SPEC-VERBS-SELECTION has an acceptance SPEC-VERBS-SELECTION-AC1 that `spec check specs` never lists, even though it is validated by the grammar and selectable by `spec list`/`assemble`. A reader of `check` therefore cannot tell an absent acceptance from an unlisted one.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: `spec check <corpus>` lists acceptance blocks that resolve, or states explicitly which kinds it reports (a `kinds` field) so absence is not ambiguous.\nPASS: a test asserts the reported node set for the shipped corpus equals the set of requirement/verification/acceptance ids that validate, with the kind of each node.\nPASS: the change does not alter `status` semantics: a corpus that validated before still validates, and an acceptance-only dangling reference still refuses.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.563106+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T21:03:54.563106+00:00", "foreman_note": null, "capability_tags": [], "depends_on": []}
