 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-165", "title": "[WIRE] Factory wiring: every dispatched worker brief embeds auger spec context --task output", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b45b3b5efcc9a48db2db7116cbf3499c7a3635f9a6c2ad050a58875d5234d919", "evidence": [{"run_id": "7d9ea575", "ts": "2026-11-14T08:06:16.671018+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "The spec context/assemble verbs exist and passed judged runs (AUG-121/122) but NO factory foreman calls them at build time: briefs are still authored from the row text alone. Wire it: on dispatch, the foreman runs `auger spec context --task <row-id>` against the project spec root and embeds the selected blocks (or the structured unscoped/ambiguous answer with its exclusion reasons) in the worker brief.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "A dispatched brief for a task with spec references contains the context-selected blocks verbatim with byte counts; a task with NO spec references produces a brief WITHOUT an empty context section; an ambiguous/unscoped result surfaces in the tick report rather than silently passing.\n\nPROOF: `PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH python3 -m pytest tests/test_brief_spec_context.py -q` \u2192 0 failed, covering the three outcome classes (blocks emitted verbatim + per-block byte count == len(text.encode()); no-context \u2192 0-byte section; ambiguous \u2192 exit 3 naming candidates).\nPROOF: `PATH=$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH python3 scripts/brief_spec_context.py --row AUG-165 --spec-root specs --repo-root $PWD | wc -c` \u2192 0 with exit 0 and stderr naming unknown-task (a row with no spec references must not emit an empty section).\nPROOF: with a corpus carrying a `<task>` block for the row, the emitted section contains that block's text byte-identically and its byte count.\nPROOF: `grep -c test_brief_spec_context tests/gate.sh` \u2192 1 and `bash -n tests/gate.sh` \u2192 rc 0 (the new test file is a gate arm, not an orphan).\nPROOF: `grep -c brief_spec_context ~/.he