 {"status": "complete", "id": "REVIEW-AUGER-006", "title": "smoke teardown rmtrees the namespace before checking DELETE status: a 409 orphans the registry row (AUG-117 recurrence)", "detail": {"fingerprint": "b5ea41def1006b6c2ada07f78d12fed32889437a431727fd36866c72a48c341e", "evidence": [{"run_id": "e273af1b", "ts": "2026-11-15T16:13:19.283134+00:00"}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured live during the 2026-11-11 review: tests/smoke.sh:62-66 calls auger.delete_namespace(ns, retries=1), then runs shutil.rmtree unconditionally, then inspects the status. On HTTP 409 (substrate lock / non-empty) the directory is destroyed and the mapping survives; the script prints 'teardown skipped'. Both throwaway namespaces from that review are still listed by GET /api/namespaces while only one has a directory on disk. AUG-117 describes this exact failure mode and is marked complete.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: tests/smoke.sh treats 409 like 429 (bounded backoff, re-enter) and does not call shutil.rmtree unless the DELETE returned 200 or 404. PASS: a run of 'bash tests/smoke.sh <ns>' on a substrate holding a sibling suite's lock leaves zero rows in GET /api/namespaces and zero directories under the substrate root \u2014 verified by listing both after the run and quoting the two empty results on the row. PASS: the two existing leftovers (auger-smoke-rv2314, auger-smoke-rvsmoke) are removed and the removal quoted. FAIL: any code path where rmtree runs before the status check.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-12T00:39:50.968237+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-15T16:13:19.283134+00:00", "foreman_note": "pytest proof 2026-11-12T00:33Z: the project's own suite reproduces this \u2014 1 failed, 719 passed, 2 skipped, 3 errors in 919.00s. Failure test_no_test_namespace_survives_the_suite + teardown error both say: DELETE returned 409 {'code':'CONFLICT'} 'Push in flight ... Retry after it completes' while tests/test_auger.py